    <color name="gold_deep">#FFB9822F</color>
    <color name="gold">#FFD9A441</color>
    <!-- Settings press feedback: the brand gold at 20% alpha, used by the
         masked ripple on the gear plates. Low enough that the press reads as
         a touch, not as a state change (the gold RING is the state). -->
    <color name="gold_press">#33D9A441</color>
    <!-- Owner order 2026-10-22 (the search highlight): a typing match is
         lit in gold, and the exact match carries a brighter plate than a
         prefix match, so HUBC is lit hardest of all the moment the last
         letter of HUBC lands. Both are the same brand gold, at two
         intensities, over the field's dark plate. -->
    <color name="gold_match">#59D9A441</color>
    <color name="gold_bright">#FFF8CE66</color>
    <color name="orange_logo">#FFE58142</color>
    <color name="crimson_logo">#FF882F48</color>
    <color name="green">#FF2FAE6F</color>
    <color name="green_hi">#FF43C98A</color>
    <color name="red">#FFC14A52</color>
    <!-- The status light's own palette (owner order 2026-10-13, third note;
         owner order 2026-10-16, fourth note): the ONLINE beacon is the brand
         green in three weights, and since the 2026-10-16 note the OFFLINE one
         is the SAME three weights in red, because the owner asked for the
         offline light to be the online light in red rather than a hollow
         ring: outside, a thin halo; inside it, a filled disc; inside that, a
         solid ball. Named here rather than left as raw hex inside the two
         drawables, so "the online light is green and the offline light is red"
         is one fact with one home, and the two beacons differ by colour alone
         (plus the breath, which only the live one is allowed to have). -->
    <color name="green_halo">#662FAE6F</color>
    <color name="green_glow">#3343C98A</color>
    <color name="red_ring">#59C14A52</color>
    <color name="red_core">#CCC14A52</color>
    <!-- The red ball inside the red disc: the same relationship the green
         core has to its glow, one step brighter than the brand red so it
         reads as a lit centre rather than as a flat dot. -->
    <color name="red_hi">#FFD65F66</color>
    <color name="teal">#FF4A9C95</color>
    <!-- teal_bright remains the tagline's neighbour colour in the header
         lockup. The Karachi clock left it on 2026-10-22: owner order, the
         date and time are read in the green the card's own UP percentage
         is read in (R.color.green), one fact stated at the only place it
         is drawn rather than as a third green invented for the line. -->
    <color name="teal_bright">#FF63B7AE</color>
    <color name="text_soft">#FFB9A6C2</color>
    <color name="text_bright">#FFF0EAF4</color>
    <color name="field_bg">#FF120A16</color>
    <color name="green_soft">#FF1E3F30</color>
    <color name="red_soft">#FF3F2226</color>
    <!-- The OFFLINE tile's gradient (owner order 2026-10-19: a darker, more
         prominent red). Two ends, top to bottom, plus the hairline that closes
         it. White ink on the lighter end is about 10:1, so the word keeps
         passing body-text contrast at the top of the gradient as well as the
         bottom; the beacon and the word still carry the state, never the
         colour alone. -->
    <color name="red_deep">#FF8E1F1F</color>
    <color name="red_deep_edge">#FF561010</color>
    <color name="red_deep_line">#FFC04545</color>
    <color name="on_red">#FFFDF3F3</color>
    <!-- The ONLINE gradient (owner order 2026-10-20): the OFFLINE tile's
         shape in the brand green. Two ends plus the closing hairline, and
         white ink on the lighter end stays well past body-text contrast. -->
    <color name="green_deep">#FF1B6B45</color>
    <color name="green_deep_edge">#FF0E3D27</color>
    <color name="green_deep_line">#FF4FC08D</color>
    <color name="orb_ai_layer_shadow_outer">#0A99CCFA</color>
